      "notes": "MN 116:6.23 names Ānanda, Nanda and Upananda among twelve independent Buddhas. The verse leaves the count for each name unstated. Ānanda 06 supplies the four and cites the Apadāna for the cremation. The page citation for Ānanda 01 also lands here, though the monk appears in MN 115. AN 1.219–223 names him foremost in five respects. DN 16:5.15.2–3 identifies the attendant, while the separately tappable ānande in DN 16:4.7.1 and 4.12.1 names the shrine at Bhoganagara. A single DN 16 identification would mislabel those taps. AN 4.180:1.1 has the compound ānandacetiye. Its only standalone Ānando is in the chapter summary at 10.2, referring back to AN 4.174, so AN 4.180 is unassigned. The commentary supplies the yakkha in Ānanda 09. The two discourses name only his shrine, and the shrine citation also spills into AN 4.178–179. The packet misses Bhadda addressing the monk as āvuso ānanda in SN 45.19 and 45.20, both at 1.2 and 1.7. Sujato omits the name there."
